  "raw_text": "\n\nBrowse Program Information\n\n\n\n\n\n\nAcademic Program:\tB.A. in Early Childhood Education\nAcademic Year:\t2024\nLanguage:\t\nEnglish\nSimplified Chinese\nTraditional Chinese\n\n\n\nLearning Outcomes\nStudy Scheme\n \n\n\t\n\nEarly Childhood Education\n\nApplicable to students admitted in 2024-25\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\n\n\n \n\nMajor Programme Requirement (for Higher Diploma holders admitted to senior-year places)\n\n \n\n\n\n\nStudents are required to complete a minimum of 55 units of courses as follows:\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\t\n\n \n\n\t\n\nUnits\n\n\n\n\n1.\n\n\t\n\nRequired Courses:\n\n\t\n\n \n\n\n\n\n(a)\n\n\t\n\nEducational Studies\n\n\t\n\n \n\n\n\n\n \n\n\t\n\nEDUC2120, 2220, 2240\n\n\t\n\n8\n\n\n\n\n(b)\n\n\t\n\nSubject Knowledge\n\n\t\n\n \n\n\n\n\n \n\n\t\n\nCHED3160, 4120, 4140, 4220[a], 4340[a], 4350[a], 4360, 4410, 4510, 4530\n\n\t\n\n29\n\n\n\n\n(c)\n\n\t\n\nResearch Experience\n\n\t\n\n \n\n\n\n\n \n\n\t\n\nCHED4320[a], 4540[a]\n\n\t\n\n7\n\n\n\n\n(d)\n\n\t\n\nInternship\n\n\t\n\n \n\n\n\n\n \n\n\t\n\nCHED4550[a]\n\n\t\n\n3\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\t\n\n \n\n\t\n\n \n\n\n\n\n2.\n\n\t\n\nElective Courses:\n\n\t\n\n \n\n\n\n\n \n\n\t\n\n8 units of courses chosen from the following:\n\n\t\n\n \n\n\n\n\n \n\n\t\n\nBECE3130#, CHED4150, 4210, 4310[a], 4330, 4370, 4520, EDUC2210, 3150, 3200, 3270, 3280, 3290, MUSC2545#, SPED3920\n\n\t\n\n8\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\t\n\nTotal:\n\n\t\n\n55\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\t\n\n \n\n\t\n\n \n\n\n\n\nExplanatory Notes:\n\n\n\n\n1.\n\n\t\n\nCHED, EDUC and SPED courses at 2000 and above level as included in the Major Programme Requirement as well as those labeled as # will be included in the calculation of Major GPA for honours classification.\n\n\n\n\n[a]\n\n\t\n\nCapstone courses\n\n\n\n\n \n\n\t\n\n \n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n\t\n\nRecommended Course Pattern\n\n\t\n\nUnits\n\n\n\n\nFirst Year of\n\nAttendance\n\n\t\n\n1st term\n\n\t\n\n \n\n\n\n\nMajor Required: CHED3160, 4360, EDUC2240\n\n\t\n\n9\n\n\n\n\nMajor Elective(s): 1 course\n\n\t\n\n2-3\n\n\n\n\n2nd term\n\n\t\n\n \n\n\n\n\nMajor Required: CHED4120, 4220, 4320, EDUC2120, 2220\n\n\t\n\n14\n\n\n\n\nMajor Elective(s): 1 course\n\n\t\n\n2-3\n\n\n\n\nSecond Year of Attendance\n\n\t\n\n1st term\n\n\t\n\n \n\n\n\n\nMajor Required: CHED4340, 4410, 4510, 4530\n\n\t\n\n11\n\n\n\n\nMajor Elective(s): 1 course\n\n\t\n\n2-3\n\n\n\n\n2nd term\n\n\t\n\n \n\n\n\n\nMajor Required: CHED4140, 4350, 4540, 4550\n\n\t\n\n13\n\n\n\n\nMajor Elective(s): 0-1 course\n\n\t\n\n0-3\n\n\n\n\nTotal:\n\n\t\n\n55\n\n\n\n\n \n\nCourse List\n\n \n\n\n\n\nCourse Code\n\n\t\n\nCourse Title\n\n\t\n\nUnit(s)\n\n\n\n\nBECE3130\n\n\t\n\nArt Therapy in Kindergarten Settings\n\n\t\n\n3\n\n\n\n\nCHED3160\n\n\t\n\nChildren’s Play in Early Childhood Education\n\n\t\n\n3\n\n\n\n\nCHED4120\n\n\t\n\nLanguage and Literacy Development in Young Children\n\n\t\n\n3\n\n\n\n\nCHED4140\n\n\t\n\nMaths, Science, and Tech Experiences in Early Childhood\n\n\t\n\n3\n\n\n\n\nCHED4150\n\n\t\n\nChildren’s Literature\n\n\t\n\n2\n\n\n\n\nCHED4210\n\n\t\n\nLeadership and Management in Early Childhood Settings\n\n\t\n\n3\n\n\n\n\nCHED4220\n\n\t\n\nHome-School-Community Collaboration for School Development\n\n\t\n\n3\n\n\n\n\nCHED4310\n\n\t\n\nAesthetic Experience and Creative Expressions in Early Childhood\n\n\t\n\n3\n\n\n\n\nCHED4320\n\n\t\n\nIntroduction to Educational Research\n\n\t\n\n3\n\n\n\n\nCHED4330\n\n\t\n\nPersonal Growth of Teachers\n\n\t\n\n2\n\n\n\n\nCHED4340\n\n\t\n\nSupporting Preschool Children with Special Educational Needs\n\n\t\n\n3\n\n\n\n\nCHED4350\n\n\t\n\nAssessment for the Development and Learning of Young Children\n\n\t\n\n3\n\n\n\n\nCHED4360\n\n\t\n\nAdvanced Study of Early Childhood Development\n\n\t\n\n3\n\n\n\n\nCHED4370\n\n\t\n\nCounselling Young Children\n\n\t\n\n2\n\n\n\n\nCHED4410\n\n\t\n\nFundamental Movement Skill and Rhythmic Activity for Young Children\n\n\t\n\n3\n\n\n\n\nCHED4510\n\n\t\n\nValues Education in Early Childhood Education\n\n\t\n\n2\n\n\n\n\nCHED4520\n\n\t\n\nGuided Study in Issues of Child Development\n\n\t\n\n3\n\n\n\n\nCHED4530\n\n\t\n\nContemporary Issues in Early Childhood Education\n\n\t\n\n3\n\n\n\n\nCHED4540\n\n\t\n\nResearch Project\n\n\t\n\n4\n\n\n\n\nCHED4550\n\n\t\n\nInternship\n\n\t\n\n3\n\n\n\n\nEDUC2120\n\n\t\n\nPrinciples and Implementation of Curriculum and Instructional Design\n\n\t\n\n3\n\n\n\n\nEDUC2210\n\n\t\n\nEducation and Society in Hong Kong\n\n\t\n\n2\n\n\n\n\nEDUC2220\n\n\t\n\nEducational Thought\n\n\t\n\n2\n\n\n\n\nEDUC2240\n\n\t\n\nUnderstanding Schooling and Education Policy in Hong Kong\n\n\t\n\n3\n\n\n\n\nEDUC3150\n\n\t\n\nGlobal Dialogues on Education for Sustainable Development in the Curriculum\n\n\t\n\n2\n\n\n\n\nEDUC3200\n\n\t\n\nDeveloping Intercultural Competence: Experiential Learning\n\n\t\n\n3\n\n\n\n\nEDUC3270\n\n\t\n\nEngendering Education\n\n\t\n\n2\n\n\n\n\nEDUC3280\n\n\t\n\nAn Introduction to Moral and Citizenship Education\n\n\t\n\n2\n\n\n\n\nEDUC3290\n\n\t\n\nMeaning Concerns, Life and Death Education\n\n\t\n\n2\n\n\n\n\nMUSC2545\n\n\t\n\nMusic Therapy\n\n\t\n\n2\n\n\n\n\nSPED3920\n\n\t\n\nHuman Growth and Health Education\n\n\t\n\n3\n\n \n\n\n \n\nStudy Scheme\n\n\nLearning Outcomes\n \n\n\t\n\n \n\n1.\n\n\t\n\nMajor Programme:\n\n\n\n\nUpon completion of the Programme, graduates of the B.A. Programme in Early Childhood Education will be able to:\n\n\n\n\n1.\n\n\t\n\nacquire knowledge on understanding the central concepts, tools of inquiry, and structures of early childhood education;\n\n\n\n\n2.\n\n\t\n\ndesign curriculum and instructional plans based on children's diverse abilities;\n\n\n\n\n3.\n\n\t\n\napply a variety of instructional strategies to encourage the development of curiosity, creativity, problem-solving and performance skills in children;\n\n\n\n\n4.\n\n\t\n\nacquire knowledge and skills on a variety of formal and informal assessment strategies, and to use various assessment strategies to evaluate and ensure the continuous all-round development of young learners;\n\n\n\n\n5.\n\n\t\n\ndemonstrate an understanding of the basic organizational and managerial theories, and ways to adopt appropriate strategies to contribute, independently and collegially, to the quality of their schools to the benefit of children, parents, the community;\n\n\n\n\n6.\n\n\t\n\nrecognize the complex characteristics of young children, young children's families and communities, and to appreciate respectful and reciprocal relationships that support children's development and learning; and\n\n\n\n\n7.\n\n\t\n\ndevelop themselves to be innovative reflective practitioners who continually evaluate the effects of their choices and who actively research and implement new methods and seek out opportunities to grow professionally.\n\n \n\n \n\n\n"
